 "_about": "Street center lines read by eye off the 1952 Sanborn sheets, volume 3 (https://www.loc.gov/item/sanborn09064_018/), in pixels of the 50% scan [u, v], at the streets' printed names and the middles of their printed widths, read on crops with a 50 px grid (Claude, November 18, 2026). Carried to the ground by each sheet's fit in geo1952.json (residuals in trace.md: 1.1-3.6 m mean per sheet), so a line is good to about the sheet's residual plus 1-2 m of reading. Where a street runs on two sheets the first sheet read wins (streets52_features.py). Names as printed; '(Walker)' and '(Tazewell)' are the sheet's own second names.",
